WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.910
Sunday night, second week of calving.

00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:09.340
The roster for the week has to be on the
shed wall before the five o'clock milking.

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:14.150
It's all there. Who's off,
who can't do Thursday afternoon,

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:18.900
when the relief milker's free.
It's just in a mess.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:26.630
Give ChatGPT, Copilot, Gemini or
Claude the availability and the rules.

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:30.230
Two on every milking.
Ben always paired up.

00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:35.280
A minute later you've got a clean roster,
and a message for the staff group chat.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:42.010
Now look at Sunday afternoon.
The roster says Tom, the relief milker.

00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:45.010
Your note says Tom hasn't confirmed.

00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:49.530
The slot was empty and his name was
close by, so the AI filled it in.

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:53.360
It looks finished, but it's a guess.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:59.170
So ask for gaps, not guesses. Tell it to
write "uncovered" when nobody's free,

00:00:59.210 --> 00:01:04.340
and check every name against your
note before the roster goes up.

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:09.130
It's the same with a neighbour
spray notice or the shed notebook.

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:13.230
If the start time isn't set,
the draft says confirm.

00:01:13.270 --> 00:01:18.300
If the seal swap is planned for Saturday,
the log doesn't call it done.

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:26.780
AI does the drafting. The facts,
and the final say, stay with you.
